<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-banana-and-strawberry-smoothie-ingredients">Banana and Strawberry Smoothie Ingredients</h2>



<p>You&rsquo;ll need only <strong>four basic ingredients</strong> to make this banana strawberry smoothie recipe. I have listed all the ingredients in the recipe card below, but below are some helpful notes to make it your own.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/smoothie-with-yogurt-strawberry-banana.jpg" alt="Ingredients for the recipe from the top view." class="wp-image-81652" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/smoothie-with-yogurt-strawberry-banana.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/smoothie-with-yogurt-strawberry-banana-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/smoothie-with-yogurt-strawberry-banana-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/smoothie-with-yogurt-strawberry-banana-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/smoothie-with-yogurt-strawberry-banana-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/smoothie-with-yogurt-strawberry-banana.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Fresh strawberries:</strong> When they&rsquo;re in season, I always go for fresh strawberries. They are naturally sweet, and I never feel the need to add extra sugar. If you&rsquo;re making this in the off-season, frozen strawberries work too. Just be aware that your smoothie will be thicker, and you might need to add more milk to adjust the consistency.</p>



<p><strong>Banana:</strong> Using a frozen banana gives this smoothie a creamy texture and chills it without needing ice. If you only have a fresh banana, that&rsquo;s fine too. I usually go for a ripe, soft banana since it&rsquo;s sweeter and helps avoid adding any sweeteners.</p>



<p><strong>Yogurt: </strong>Any type of yogurt will work here. I usually use plain or <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/vanilla-yogurt/">vanilla yogurt that I make from plain yogurt</a>. Plain Greek yogurt is a good option if you like a thicker smoothie, though you may need to add a little extra milk. For a dairy-free or vegan smoothie, plant-based yogurts like cashew or almond yogurt are great. Personally, I like cashew yogurt because it has a more neutral taste that doesn&rsquo;t overpower the fruit.</p>



<p><strong>Milk: </strong>You can use regular or any plant-based/dairy-free milk you have on hand. <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/how-to-make-almond-milk/">Almond milk</a>, oat milk, or soy milk are all good choices and blend well with the other ingredients.</p>


<div class="su-note" style="border-color:#d9d8d7;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;"><div class="su-note-inner su-u-clearfix su-u-trim" style="background-color:#f3f2f1;border-color:#ffffff;color:#000;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;">



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-optional-add-ins">Optional Add-Ins</h3>



<p>This strawberry banana smoothie recipe is simple and satisfying as is, but it&rsquo;s also easy to customize. Here are a few optional add-ins you can try to make it your own:</p>



<p><strong>Sweeteners:</strong> I find the smoothie sweet enough with just fresh fruit, but if you want a little extra, a drizzle of honey or maple syrup works well. I often use local honey, especially during allergy season.</p>



<p><strong>Protein:</strong> If you want to turn this smoothie into a more filling breakfast or post-workout snack, adding protein is a great option. A scoop of your favorite protein powder blends in easily, or you can use a tablespoon of peanut butter (or almond butter) for extra creaminess and a touch of nutty taste.</p>



<p><strong>Superfoods:</strong> While optional, adding a spoonful of chia seeds, ground flax seeds, or hemp seeds is an easy way to include a bit more fiber and protein. The good news is that they mix in well and do not change the taste much.</p>



<p><strong>Greens: </strong>A small handful of spinach or baby kale blends in well and is an easy way to add more vegetables to your day. The fresh fruit does a great job masking the taste, especially if you&rsquo;re making this for picky eaters (or trying to sneak in some greens yourself).</p>



<p><strong>Flavor boosters: </strong>For an extra layer of warmth and sweetness, a tiny splash of vanilla extract can truly elevate this smoothie. It&rsquo;s my secret touch that makes it taste a bit more gourmet without any extra effort.</p>


</div></div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-a-strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt">How To Make a Strawberry Banana Smoothie with Yogurt?</h2>



<p>Making this smoothie is as simple as it gets. It comes together in just a few minutes, and cleanup is minimal&mdash;perfect for busy mornings or a quick afternoon pick-me-up.</p>



<p><strong>Grab your blender:</strong> If you have a high-powered blender like a Vitamix, this is a great time to use it. That said, a standard blender will work just fine for this banana and strawberry smoothie.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="738" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/make-a-strawberry-banana-smoothie.jpg" alt="A collage of images showing how to make banana strawberry smoothie recipe." class="wp-image-81653" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/make-a-strawberry-banana-smoothie.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/make-a-strawberry-banana-smoothie-350x215.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/make-a-strawberry-banana-smoothie-768x472.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/make-a-strawberry-banana-smoothie-400x246.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/make-a-strawberry-banana-smoothie-150x92.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/make-a-strawberry-banana-smoothie.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Add ingredients</strong>: For best results, start with the softer ingredients. Add your liquids and softer ingredients, meaning your yogurt, milk, and fresh strawberries (and of course any of the optional add-ins, if using). Then top it with the frozen banana. This layering helps the blades move freely without getting stuck and blend everything more easily. This is especially helpful if you do not have a high-powered blender because &ldquo;the vortex&rdquo; that the softer ingredients create helps break the fruit more efficiently without overworking your blender.</p>



<p><strong>Blend: </strong>Start on a low speed to help break down the fruit gradually and avoid splashes, then increase to high and blend until everything is thoroughly combined and smooth to your liking. If you like your smoothie thinner, add a splash more milk and blend again.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Taste and adjust: </strong>Give it a quick taste. If you want more strawberry or banana flavor, feel free to toss in a little extra and blend again. Smoothies are wonderfully flexible, so make it your own according to your taste.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-pin-title="Strawberry Banana Smoothie" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt.jpg" alt="Strawberry banana smoothie in a glass garnished with a strawberry." class="wp-image-81654" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/strawberry-banana-smoothie-with-yogurt.jpg"></figure>


<div class="su-note" style="border-color:#d9d8d7;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;"><div class="su-note-inner su-u-clearfix su-u-trim" style="background-color:#f3f2f1;border-color:#ffffff;color:#000;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;">



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-helpful-tips">Helpful Tips</h2>



<p><strong>Using ice:</strong> I avoid using ice in my smoothies to prevent diluting the rich fresh fruit flavors. That said, if you&rsquo;re using fresh bananas, a small amount of ice can help chill the smoothie without changing its consistency too much.</p>



<p><strong>Consistency and texture:</strong> This is where you have so much creative control. If you prefer your smoothie thick and creamy, blend less or add a bit more fruit. For a thinner, smoother texture, just add more milk or yogurt.</p>



<p><strong>Quick blender clean up:</strong> This strawberry banana smoothie takes just 5 minutes to make, but let&rsquo;s be honest, cleaning the blender often takes longer. Here&rsquo;s my go-to trick: fill the empty blender with warm water and a drop of dish soap, blend for about 30 seconds, then rinse. That&rsquo;s it. No scrubbing needed!</p>


</div></div>
