<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-faqs">FAQs</h2>



<div class="schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block"><div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1748033648278"><strong class="schema-faq-question">How do you freeze bananas to make this smoothie?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Peel and slice a ripe banana and place the slices on a sheet pan lined with parchment paper in a single layer. Place in the freezer for at least 3 hours or overnight.</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1748033552908"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Can I use a fresh banana instead of frozen?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Yes, you can. However, keep in mind that using frozen bananas make the smoothie creamy without using ice. If using fresh, feel free to use a handful of ice to make it cold.</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1748033524686"><strong class="schema-faq-question">How can I make my smoothie thicker or thinner?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Add more fruit to make it thicker or more liquid to make it thinner.</p> </div> </div>


